        ":question/id": "e914c5f1-73b1-5b4b-b68d-637aec2b2d11",
        ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{x}{x^{2} + 8}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x).$\n\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=x^{2} + 8,$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u^{\\prime}(x)&=1,\\\\v^{\\prime}(x)&=2 x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}(x)&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^2}\\\\ &=\\frac{(1)\\cdot (x^{2} + 8)-(x)\\cdot (2 x)}{(x^{2} + 8)^2}\\\\ &=\\frac{8 - x^{2}}{\\left(x^{2} + 8\\right)^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{8 - x^{2}}{\\left(x^{2} + 8\\right)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
